Each matrix must be a non-empty list of non-empty, equally sized row lists. Entries must be finite integers or floats, excluding bools. The number of columns in `left` must equal the number of rows in `right`; otherwise raise `ValueError`. Return their conventional matrix product as a newly allocated list of independently allocated rows. Neither input may be mutated or aliased by the result. All malformed inputs raise `ValueError`.

